---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How we compare labs — editorial policy"
  description="Where our prices come from, how often they update, how rankings work, and how to report an error."
  path="/editorial-policy/"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'How we compare', path: '/editorial-policy/' }]}
>
  <div class="prose-tight max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-extrabold sm:text-3xl">How we compare</h1>

    <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-bold">Where prices come from</h2>
    <p>
      Automated checks read each lab's public website — the same pages you'd
      see as a customer. We record the listed price, MRP, home-collection fee,
      any platform charges, and coupon codes the lab itself advertises. Fees a
      lab only reveals at checkout are marked "shown at checkout" rather than
      guessed.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-bold">How often prices update</h2>
    <p>
      Nightly checks cover a rotating set of labs, so every lab is re-verified
      at least weekly. Each row shows its own "verified" date. Rows older than
      14 days get a stale marker; older than 30 days, we pull them off the page
      entirely.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-bold">How rankings work</h2>
    <p>
      Default sort is lowest total payable: listed price, plus collection and
      platform fees, minus advertised coupons. You can re-sort by coverage or
      price-per-parameter. No lab can pay to move up; if sponsored placement
      ever exists, it will be labelled on the listing itself.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-bold">How package contents are verified</h2>
    <p>
      We map each package's published contents onto standard panels (CBC, lipid
      profile, liver function and so on). Where our verified count differs from
      the lab's claimed count, both numbers are shown. Mappings a human has
      checked carry a "verified" mark; the rest are automated and flagged for
      review.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-bold">Ratings</h2>
    <p>
      Star ratings come from Google, the Play Store and the App Store, each
      labelled with its source. We don't collect or edit reviews ourselves and
      we don't fold ratings into the price ranking.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-bold">Mistakes</h2>
    <p>
      Prices change and scrapers miss things. If a number here doesn't match
      the lab's site, <a href="/contact/" class="text-navy underline">tell us</a> —
      corrections ship within a working day. Labs can use the same address for
      data disputes or removal requests.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
